{"id": 547630, "title": "CVE-2019-5435: An integer overflow found in /lib/urlapi.c", "submitted": "2019-04-24", "source_url": "https://hackerone.com/reports/547630", "excerpt": "## Summary:\n\nlibcurl contains a heap-based buffer overrun in /lib/urlapi.c. A similiar issue to CVE-2018-14618.\n\n## Steps To Reproduce:\n\n### analysis\n\nI found a potential integer overflow which may lead to a buffer overrun in /curl/lib/urlapi.c. In function `seturl`, urllen was multiplied by 2 and then passed to malloc. So an integer overflow will happen when the url is as long as 2GB in a 32 bit OS. \n\n```c\nstatic CURLUcode seturl(const char *url, CURLU *u, unsigned int flags)\n{\n  char *path;\n  bool path_alloced = FALSE;\n  char *hostname;\n  char *query = NULL;\n  char *fragment = NULL;\n  CURLUcode result;\n  bool url_has_scheme = FALSE;\n  char schemebuf[MAX_SCHEME_LEN];\n  char *schemep = NULL;\n  size_t schemelen = 0;\n  size_t urllen;\n  const struct Curl_handler *h = NULL;\n\n  if(!url)\n    return CURLUE_MALFORMED_INPUT;\n\n  /*************************************************************\n   * Parse the URL.\n   ************************************************************/\n  /* allocate scratch area */\n  urllen = strlen(url);\n  path = u->scratch = malloc(urllen * 2 + 2); <= overflow here\n```\n\nThe url was passed by `parseurl` to `seturl`.\n\n```c\nstatic CURLUcode parseurl(const char *url, CURLU *u, unsigned int flags)\n{\n  CURLUcode result = seturl(url, u, flags);\n  if(result) {\n    free_urlhandle(u);\n    memset(u, 0, sizeof(struct Curl_URL));\n  }\n  return result;\n}\n```\n\nAnd the `parseurl` was called when do `curl_url_set` and execute the parse of url.  If someone use libcurl to code, and call `curl_url_set` with a extreme long url, it might be triggered.\n\n```c \nCURLUcode curl_url_set(CURLU *u, CURLUPart what,\n                       const char *part, unsigned int flags)\n......\ncase CURLUPART_URL: {\n    /*\n     * Allow a new URL to replace the existing (if any) contents.\n     *\n     * If the existing contents is enough for a URL, allow a relative URL to\n     * replace it.\n     */\n    CURLUcode result;\n    char *oldurl;\n    char *redired_url;\n    CURLU *handle2;\n\n    if(Curl_is_absolute_url(part, NULL, MAX_SCHEME_LEN)) {\n      handle2 = curl_url();\n      if(!handle2)\n        return CURLUE_OUT_OF_MEMORY;\n      result = parseurl(part, handle2, flags); <= call parseurl\n      if(!result)\n        mv_urlhandle(handle2, u);\n      else\n        curl_url_cleanup(handle2);\n      return result;\n    }\n```\n\n## Impact\n\nIt might leads to a crash or some other impact.", "excerpt_truncated": false, "final": "likely_valid", "final_label": "Code supports the claim", "tone": "good", "explain": "The code supports the reported flaw. A maintainer should review its impact and decide what to do next.", "confidence": 0.7, "judge_verdict": "likely_valid", "receipts_override": "", "policy_section": "", "grounding": {"verdict": "grounded", "rev": "e7d3f65ab95a", "rev_source": "master on 2019-04-24", "counts": {"grounded": 13, "ungrounded_strong": 0, "ungrounded_medium": 0}, "problems": []}, "summary": "An integer overflow in curl's seturl function may cause a heap-based buffer overrun when processing URLs up to 2GB in length on 32-bit systems.", "claims": [{"id": "C1", "kind": "flaw", "text": "urllen was multiplied by 2 and then passed to malloc, causing integer overflow when url length reaches 2GB on 32-bit OS", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The code computes urllen * 2 + 2 in size_t and passes it to malloc. On 32-bit systems where size_t is 32-bit unsigned, this multiplication wraps modulo 2^32 when urllen exceeds ~2.1GB, causing malloc to allocate a small buffer instead of the intended large one.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/urlapi.c", "line": 634, "note": "urllen declared as size_t", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/urlapi.c", "line": 644, "note": "urllen = strlen(url); returns size_t", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/urlapi.c", "line": 645, "note": "malloc(urllen * 2 + 2); multiplication in size_t arithmetic, wraps on 32-bit when urllen > ~2GB", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C2", "kind": "location", "text": "in function seturl in /lib/urlapi.c", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The function seturl is defined at line 622 in lib/urlapi.c and contains the allocation at line 645.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/urlapi.c", "line": 622, "note": "static CURLUcode seturl(const char *url, CURLU *u, unsigned int flags)", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C3", "kind": "trigger", "text": "when a URL of length 2GB is processed on a 32-bit OS", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "No bounds check on the full URL length exists before the multiplication. The trigger condition (2GB URL on 32-bit) is theoretically reachable via the public API curl_url_set with an absolute URL.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/urlapi.c", "line": 644, "note": "urllen = strlen(url); no length check before multiplication", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/urlapi.c", "line": 1229, "note": "curl_url_set calls Curl_is_absolute_url which only checks scheme length (MAX_SCHEME_LEN), not total URL length", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C4", "kind": "impact", "text": "may lead to a crash or buffer overrun", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "After the integer overflow, malloc returns a tiny buffer. Subsequent pointer arithmetic (path[urllen + 1]) and writes (hostname[0] = 0) use the original huge urllen value, causing out-of-bounds heap access — a buffer overrun that can crash or corrupt memory.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/urlapi.c", "line": 645, "note": "malloc(urllen * 2 + 2) returns undersized buffer after wrap", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/urlapi.c", "line": 649, "note": "hostname = &path[urllen + 1]; pointer arithmetic with huge urllen", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/urlapi.c", "line": 650, "note": "hostname[0] = 0; writes to wrapped pointer location", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C5", "kind": "reproduction", "text": "use curl_url_set with an extreme long URL to trigger parseurl and seturl", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The call chain curl_url_set -> parseurl -> seturl is present and reachable when the input is an absolute URL. An attacker controlling the URL string passed to curl_url_set can trigger the flaw.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/urlapi.c", "line": 1114, "note": "CURLUcode curl_url_set(CURLU *u, CURLUPart what, const char *part, unsigned int flags)", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/urlapi.c", "line": 1229, "note": "if(Curl_is_absolute_url(part, NULL, MAX_SCHEME_LEN)) { handle2 = curl_url(); result = parseurl(part, handle2, flags); }", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/urlapi.c", "line": 884, "note": "static CURLUcode parseurl(const char *url, CURLU *u, unsigned int flags) { result = seturl(url, u, flags); }", "valid": true}]}], "external_checks": [], "external_sources": [], "key_reasons": ["The integer overflow in urllen * 2 + 2 is real and present in the provided code at lib/urlapi.c:645.", "No length check guards the multiplication; the call chain curl_url_set -> parseurl -> seturl is reachable with an absolute URL.", "On 32-bit systems the wrap causes malloc to return a small buffer, and subsequent writes using the original urllen overrun the heap.", "Practical exploitability on 32-bit is limited by address-space constraints (a 2+ GB string is hard to allocate), but the flaw is a classic heap overflow via integer wrap and similar issues (e.g., CVE-2018-14618) have been treated as security vulnerabilities in curl."], "missing_info": [], "reply": "Thank you for the report. The integer overflow at lib/urlapi.c:645 (urllen * 2 + 2) is real and reachable via curl_url_set with an absolute URL. On 32-bit systems the multiplication wraps, malloc returns an undersized buffer, and later writes overrun the heap. While a 2+ GB URL is difficult to supply on 32-bit due to address-space limits, the flaw is a genuine heap buffer overrun and matches patterns we have fixed before (e.g., CVE-2018-14618). We will address it.", "code": [{"name": "lib/urlapi.c", "start": 622, "end": 782, "reason": "definition of seturl (truncated)", "rows": [{"n": 622, "text": "static CURLUcode seturl(const char *url, CURLU *u, unsigned int flags)", "notes": ["C2: static CURLUcode seturl(const char *url, CURLU *u, unsigned int flags)"]}, {"n": 623, "text": "{", "notes": []}, {"n": 624, "text": "  char *path;", "notes": []}, {"n": 625, "text": "  bool path_alloced = FALSE;", "notes": []}, {"n": 626, "text": "  char *hostname;", "notes": []}, {"n": 627, "text": "  char *query = NULL;", "notes": []}, {"n": 628, "text": "  char *fragment = NULL;", "notes": []}, {"n": 629, "text": "  CURLUcode result;", "notes": []}, {"n": 630, "text": "  bool url_has_scheme = FALSE;", "notes": []}, {"n": 631, "text": "  char schemebuf[MAX_SCHEME_LEN];", "notes": []}, {"n": 632, "text": "  char *schemep = NULL;", "notes": []}, {"n": 633, "text": "  size_t schemelen = 0;", "notes": []}, {"n": 634, "text": "  size_t urllen;", "notes": ["C1: urllen declared as size_t"]}, {"n": 635, "text": "  const struct Curl_handler *h = NULL;", "notes": []}, {"n": 636, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 637, "text": "  if(!url)", "notes": []}, {"n": 638, "text": "    return CURLUE_MALFORMED_INPUT;", "notes": []}, {"n": 639, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 640, "text": "  /*************************************************************", "notes": []}, {"n": 641, "text": "   * Parse the URL.", "notes": []}, {"n": 642, "text": "   ************************************************************/", "notes": []}, {"n": 643, "text": "  /* allocate scratch area */", "notes": []}, {"n": 644, "text": "  urllen = strlen(url);", "notes": ["C1: urllen = strlen(url); returns size_t", "C3: urllen = strlen(url); no length check before multiplication"]}, {"n": 645, "text": "  path = u->scratch = malloc(urllen * 2 + 2);", "notes": ["C1: malloc(urllen * 2 